# DEPRECATED: an older profile without a [hal] table in ferrum.toml runs this
# file. Ferrum ignores it once ferrum.toml has [hal] (docs/hal.md).
# watchdog module (always on): E-stop when the screen stops drawing.
# ferrum flips ferrum.watchdog.heartbeat once per frame it actually draws,
# and asks for a frame at least every 250 ms. If no flip arrives for 1 s
# (frozen window, hung or crashed ferrum), the oneshot drops and drives
# estop-latch.0.fault-in from mymill.hal, so the machine goes to E-stop and
# stays there until E-stop is reset from a working screen. The machine
# cannot be turned on before the screen draws.
loadrt oneshot names=ferrum-screen-watchdog
addf ferrum-screen-watchdog servo-thread
setp ferrum-screen-watchdog.width 1.0
setp ferrum-screen-watchdog.retriggerable 1
setp ferrum-screen-watchdog.rising 1
setp ferrum-screen-watchdog.falling 1
net ferrum-screen-heartbeat ferrum.watchdog.heartbeat => ferrum-screen-watchdog.in
net ferrum-screen-ok    <= ferrum-screen-watchdog.out     => ferrum.watchdog.ok
net ferrum-screen-stale <= ferrum-screen-watchdog.out-not => estop-latch.0.fault-in
